4772
06:01:44,080 --> 06:01:49,080
 So you have all your bots kind of here on the left-hand side and they're doing different things.

4773
06:01:49,080 --> 06:01:56,080
 Like we have a sales outbound bot here, we have our chief of staff, and you can message them just like you message your own teammates.

4774
06:01:56,080 --> 06:01:59,080
 And more interestingly, you can actually see them talk with each other.

4775
06:01:59,080 --> 06:02:05,080
 And I have my own Grockbot instance set up where really there's only one bot that I'm actually talking to.

4776
06:02:05,080 --> 06:02:14,080
 And so for the most part, I've kind of offloaded all that context to my chief of staff actually talking with other bots and doing that all for me.

4777
06:02:14,080 --> 06:02:22,080
 And I think some important things also to emphasize here is that bots keep their own context at a per bot level and memory,

4778
06:02:22,080 --> 06:02:25,080
 so they can really improve as you work more with them.

4779
06:02:25,080 --> 06:02:27,080
 And as you go, their memory gets better.

4780
06:02:27,080 --> 06:02:31,080
 And this is why I really emphasize you actually should be training your bots as well,

4781
06:02:31,080 --> 06:02:34,080
 depending on the task with kind of the relevant info.

4782
06:02:34,080 --> 06:02:40,080
 So set up your Slack, set up your Gmail connector, and you can actually kind of start to train it on what your voice looks like.

4783
06:02:40,080 --> 06:02:48,080
 And so specifically for Gmail, what I do is I've had it go into my Gmail and actually look at how do I actually talk to people.

