6277
07:31:38,080 --> 07:31:40,080
 So first, what is Grokbot?

6278
07:31:40,080 --> 07:31:46,080
 Grokbot is a new product that lets you hand off real work to an AI coworker.

6279
07:31:46,080 --> 07:31:53,080
 The interface looks very familiar, just like a messenger app on your phone or a computer.

6280
07:31:53,080 --> 07:31:58,080
 But under the hood, it's built to keep working after you've sent your original message.

6281
07:31:58,080 --> 07:32:04,080
 So you aren't just chatting back and forth with quick, simple one-offs here and there.

6282
07:32:04,080 --> 07:32:11,080
 You're really able to delegate a real project to Grokbot and it can go off and take it from there.

6283
07:32:11,080 --> 07:32:17,080
 One of my favorite things about Grokbot is how flexible it is to the way you work.

6284
07:32:17,080 --> 07:32:22,080
 So you can start with a single general bot to help you get set up quickly and easily.

6285
07:32:22,080 --> 07:32:29,080
 Or create a team of specialists that coordinate around the task and work in parallel on certain subtasks.

6286
07:32:29,080 --> 07:32:35,080
 And however your team operates, Grokbot can fit in and be very useful very quickly.

6287
07:32:35,080 --> 07:32:39,080
 So why Grokbot?

6288
07:32:39,080 --> 07:32:46,080
 Why does it feel like interacting with a capable coworker rather than just another AI tool?

6289
07:32:46,080 --> 07:32:48,080
 For me, there are three big reasons.

6290
07:32:48,080 --> 07:32:51,080
 First, Grokbot is always on.

6291
07:32:51,080 --> 07:32:55,080
 So by now you may have heard that Grokbots have their own computer.

6292
07:32:55,080 --> 07:33:05,080
 All that really means is that they can work without using yours, which is a little bit more powerful than you would think.

6293
07:33:05,080 --> 07:33:12,080
 So if you close your laptop or you are working on something else, your Grokbots can still finish the task you assigned them

6294
07:33:12,080 --> 07:33:18,080
 without you having to check in constantly and steer them too much or slowing down your local machine.

6295
07:33:18,080 --> 07:33:30,080
 There are also routines, which are cron jobs or event-based triggers that you can launch your Grokbots with and make them super reactive.

6296
07:33:30,080 --> 07:33:37,080
 This way you don't have to be online at the exact moment you want them to run or start working on the task.

6297
07:33:37,080 --> 07:33:41,080
 And these are super simple to set up.

6298
07:33:41,080 --> 07:33:48,080
 All you have to do is tell it, create a routine at this time or on this event, just like a normal conversation.

6299
07:33:48,080 --> 07:33:51,080
 And it will set it up for you.

6300
07:33:51,080 --> 07:33:54,080
 Second, it is really easy to use.

6301
07:33:54,080 --> 07:33:57,080
 The interface is familiar for a reason.

6302
07:33:57,080 --> 07:34:03,080
 You don't have to be an engineer that is familiar with the ins and outs of an IDE to use bots effectively.

6303
07:34:03,080 --> 07:34:09,080
 You can just talk with it normally like you would a friend or teammate on Slack.

6304
07:34:09,080 --> 07:34:12,080
 And finally, it fits how you actually work.

6305
07:34:12,080 --> 07:34:15,080
 There are already connectors for most tools you use.

6306
07:34:15,080 --> 07:34:18,080
 You just have to go into the marketplace and search for them.

6307
07:34:18,080 --> 07:34:21,080
 And there is likely one for you.

6308
07:34:21,080 --> 07:34:26,080
 So you can plug Grokbot immediately into your ticketing system,

6309
07:34:26,080 --> 07:34:34,080
 whether that's Plane, Zendesk, Intercom, where your team chats like Slack,

6310
07:34:34,080 --> 07:34:38,080
 where your knowledge base is like Notion.

6311
07:34:38,080 --> 07:34:43,080
 And then from there, you can use the bots and routines like building blocks

6312
07:34:43,080 --> 07:34:45,080
 that fit the way your team actually works.

6313
07:34:45,080 --> 07:34:51,080
 And one really powerful thing about Grokbot is if there is a missing piece,

6314
07:34:51,080 --> 07:34:55,080
 you can likely have Grokbot build it.

6315
07:34:55,080 --> 07:34:57,080
 Grokbot has access to cloud agents.

6316
07:34:57,080 --> 07:35:00,080
 So if there is something that you're missing,

6317
07:35:00,080 --> 07:35:04,080
 you can just have it tell it to spin up a cloud agent to build a certain connector

6318
07:35:04,080 --> 07:35:07,080
 or a certain thing, and it can go off and do it for you.

6319
07:35:07,080 --> 07:35:10,080
 So you can get creative and build around,

6320
07:35:10,080 --> 07:35:14,080
 and you're not stuck waiting on Eng Roadmap or a third-party vendor

6321
07:35:14,080 --> 07:35:17,080
 to add support for the thing you need.

6322
07:35:20,080 --> 07:35:21,080
 Cool.

