6341
07:36:41,080 --> 07:36:47,080
 So at scale, you may have a lot of support tickets with a ton of different customer states.

6342
07:36:47,080 --> 07:36:54,080
 And it can be really challenging to find the things you should care about in that exact moment that need your attention.

6343
07:36:54,080 --> 07:36:59,080
 GrothBot can make this a lot easier through alerting.

6344
07:36:59,080 --> 07:37:02,080
 So you can spin up a bot that looks for certain things.

6345
07:37:02,080 --> 07:37:08,080
 For example, maybe your team is hyper focused on churn this quarter.

6346
07:37:08,080 --> 07:37:17,080
 And you want to know when someone writes in that is threatening to churn that has been a customer for six months or more.

6347
07:37:17,080 --> 07:37:23,080
 Anyone on your team can spin up a GrothBot that you have connected to your ticketing system.

6348
07:37:23,080 --> 07:37:30,080
 You can just tell it to create a routine that looks through your tickets.

6349
07:37:30,080 --> 07:37:40,080
 Every hour classifies if a user is threatening to churn and has been a customer for a certain period of time.

