07:37:40,080 --> 07:37:47,080
 And then send you an alert in the Slack channel so everyone has visibility.

6351
07:37:47,080 --> 07:37:48,080
 Yeah.

6352
07:37:48,080 --> 07:38:02,080
 And another one that maybe is more powerful than you think or is harder to get to than you think is an internal question and answer agent.

6353
07:38:02,080 --> 07:38:08,080
 So if you've used other support agents, they are primarily focused on customer replies.

6354
07:38:08,080 --> 07:38:18,080
 It's surprisingly cumbersome to leverage the knowledge knowledge base you've already sort of created or accumulated to answer your own teammates questions.

6355
07:38:18,080 --> 07:38:25,080
 You may have someone in GTM that is trying to get up to speed on today's release about cloud agents.

6356
07:38:25,080 --> 07:38:38,080
 So they can come prepared to a customer call or a TSE manager looking for changes to the internal refund policy over time and if that has impacted certain customers.

6357
07:38:38,080 --> 07:38:55,080
 You have already done the hard work of creating this knowledge base of both public info so think your docs and help center as well as likely some internal info so you might have suggested operating procedures around how your teammates handle refunds.

6358
07:38:55,080 --> 07:38:56,080
 So that is not public information.

6359
07:38:56,080 --> 07:39:04,080
 You should be able to query this intelligently within Slack and GrokBot makes this really easy.

