6630
08:00:53,200 --> 08:00:58,800
 And there are ways -- I've already tried to like experiment and found ways to get that down a lot.

6631
08:00:58,800 --> 08:01:12,800
 So there are a lot of maybe low-complexity billing tickets of like a user just asking for a refund or a user asking about a certain new email they received.

6632
08:01:12,800 --> 08:01:28,200
 You can sort of bucket those, you can run a script, have it run a script to find those first or run that manually so it has more of a contained sort of set.

6633
08:01:28,200 --> 08:01:32,600
 And then have it reply all at once with the script to those tickets.

6634
08:01:32,600 --> 08:01:40,600
 And I found that I could get that down to about $0.20 a ticket for those like low-complexity tickets, which is a huge sort of change.

6635
08:01:40,600 --> 08:01:48,000
 If you've used any of the other sort of support agents, you know that like the cost per -- they usually charge per resolution.

6636
08:01:48,000 --> 08:01:54,000
 And that's easily at minimum $1, if not between $1 to $10, like order of magnitude.

6637
08:01:54,000 --> 08:02:00,000
 And if you're having humans respond to those tickets, that can be even higher -- noticeably higher.

6638
08:02:00,000 --> 08:02:04,000
